{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"evolving data stream classifier evolving data stream classifier","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md","fileName":"Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Evolving Data Stream Classifier","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Streaming and Scalable Classification]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Streaming and Scalable Classification","dataclassification.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"evolving data stream classifier evolving data stream classifier","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md","fileName":"Evolving Data Stream Classifier.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Evolving Data Stream Classifier","heading":"Evolving Data Stream Classifier","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An evolving data stream classifier adapts when the relationship between features and labels changes over time. Recent examples must influence the model more strongly when older patterns no longer describe the current process.\n\nAdaptation can use sliding windows, fading weights, change detectors, or replacement of model components. A learner that adapts too slowly preserves stale concepts, while one that adapts too quickly mistakes random variation for genuine drift.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Streaming and Scalable Classification","dataclassification.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Evolving Da